                <pb facs="1023" n="983" xml:id="pg983"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On July 20, President Truman sent
                    condolences to Crown Prince Talal, and
                        Acheson sent a message to Prime
                    Minister Samir al-Rifai. Later in the
                    day, on official information that Emir
                        Naif had been proclaimed Regent, the President sent a message to
                    him expressing regret that he should be called upon to assume the regency under
                    such unhappy circumstances. For texts of these messages, see the Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 30, 1951, page 171.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
